module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.CenteredToricTowerLiftData

/-!
# Existence of a centered toric tower lift

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé VIII, 3.2.19, p.106,
using Lemma 3.2.15 and Corollary 3.2.18
(blueprint: lem-trf-centered-toric-tower-lift-existence).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Monoscheme

/-- An equivariant normalized tower admits an ordered saturated monoscheme lift.
This is the construction part only: neither uniqueness nor terminal smoothness is asserted.

Source: ILO VIII 3.2.19, p.106, using 3.2.15 and 3.2.18
(blueprint: lem-trf-centered-toric-tower-lift-existence).

Proof: induct on the number of stages already lifted. Initially take M, with the inverse
of the specified base identification; there are no centers or arrows. Its component torus
embeddings and actions supply the initial equivariant comparison. Suppose the lift is
constructed through stage i. Pull the coherent center J_i back by the current scheme
identification. Transport its given action through the equivariant comparison. On each
component this is the ordinary torus coaction; hence toric_ideal_comparison recovers a
unique coherent monoid ideal I_i with ringIdeal I_i equal to that pulled center.
An empty monoid ideal on a component would realize to the zero ideal there. The component
is nonempty and clopen by finite_chart_components_realization, so the zero set of J_i
would contain a nonempty open set. This contradicts nowhere density. Coherence and the
common generic point of a component then imply nonempty stalks everywhere: an empty
stalk has a neighborhood generated by no sections, whereas any nonempty stalk specializes
from a nonempty generic stalk. Thus I_i is nonempty coherent.
Apply toric_blowup_comparison to construct its saturated blowup, fine and torsion free.
Its finite chart cover and monomial formulas identify its realization with the normalized
blowup of the pulled center. Transport the normalized blowup along the current scheme
isomorphism and use T.blowup to identify it over the base with the prescribed next level.
These chart maps give both the center equality and the commuting arrow square. On each
chart the original torus coaction acts by the same lattice grading, commutes with these
monomial maps, and restricts on the dense original torus to its given action. The actions
and comparisons agree on localized overlaps and glue, furnishing the equivariant field
at stage i+1 over the original base. Iterate through n stages, retaining all stages,
including unit centers; for n=0 the initial datum already is the lift. Empty M gives
empty charts and vacuous component conditions throughout. -/
theorem exists_centeredToricTowerLift (M : Fine.{u}) (hM : M.IsTorsionFree)
    (n : ℕ) (T : NormalizedTower.{u} n)
    (e₀ : T.level 0 ≅ realization (ULift.{u} ℚ) M)
    (hEquivariant : T.HasEquivariantToricCenters M e₀)
    (hNowhereDense : T.HasNowhereDenseCenters) :
    Nonempty (CenteredToricTowerLift M T e₀) := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Monoscheme
